// 7, l.28256, l.28423 item 2). PRICES, DEF-771 (MEDIUM, fails closed, off parity, made by item 7): item 7's laundered-view party at the caller is
// rooted at the whole argument and live from the holder's declaration, so a right program whose holder is written or handed on while a view through
// it is live is refused (BORROW-015). It is off parity on 29 cells (l.28423 item 2: kinds K1, the creating call's own write, and K3, the holder
// handed on; each one's by-name twin is accepted on main and on every build), and at parity on its K2 cells (a write before the view is laid),
// whose twins main refuses too. One cell per class below (m85k, w30k and w30s off parity; w30h and w30l at parity); main's own K3 case is
// `ks5_self_holder_def771.npk`. Ways out: `holder_view_def771_wayout_*_ok.npk`, each 67 on main and on row B3's build. This changes landing 177a's
// N for a laundered view (l.28266). In the form of main's prices files.
